        "Multiply the second derivative by the first derivative:\n$$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} \\times \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x + 1}} \\times \\sqrt{4x + 1} = 2$$\n$$\\text{Since this product is equal to } 2 \\text{ for all } x, \\text{ it is constant}$$"
